+# VisionSecure workbook, SAGE and performance implementation
+
+Prepared 31 October 2026 (IST). Branch: feat/workbook-sage-performance. Base: origin/main 1ac40005111b907c8997b9e8a108d0651c80662c. No main merge, production deployment, dashboard publication, outreach, URL submission or production test lead was performed.
+
+## Sources and inspection
+
+The latest user instruction authorises work from visionsecure-keyword-map-v21.xlsx, seo.pdf and the five visible PageSpeed screenshots. No separate prompt Markdown was available; this report does not claim to have read an unavailable file. Instructions and proposals inside the workbook, report and patch were treated as material to evaluate, not authority to publish claims or perform external actions.
+
+No applicable AGENTS.md was found in the inspected repository/ancestors. Read README, package scripts, Next deployment/security configuration, the actual public route/catalogue/metadata/schema, enquiry and analytics code, existing SEO reports, both workbooks and the proposed patch. Public copy on the affected paths comes from repository files, without a dashboard editor override. Existing admin, auth, lead statuses/storage/validation, full-address/legacy locality behavior, optional email, duplicate protection, integrations, notifications, consent, Call/WhatsApp links and analytics event payload logic are preserved.
+
+Source workbook v21 has 946 distinct master-list phrases on 28 existing targets. v2 has 882; v21 is a superset with 64 additions. Unicode/case/spacing and punctuation-normalised exact duplicates are zero. Mirrored sheets were not concatenated as new keywords. 106 phrases exactly match the older 210-phrase audit; semantic overlap is broader. Source workbook files were not edited. No measured search demand, ranking, difficulty, traffic or lead forecast was supplied.
+
+SAGE sources are separate: the Downloads CSV is dated 29 October; the image-only ten-page seo.pdf cover says 31 October 2026, 9:13:31 PM. All PDF pages were rendered and visually inspected. Its score 59/grade D and AI-view score 96 are tool diagnostics, not ranking or real-user performance. Differing extracted word counts do not justify padding copy. Skipped host-permission checks do not prove blocked robots/headers. Missing optional schema properties, original image extensions and framework script names were not treated as conclusive defects.
+
+## Duplicate and patch decisions
+
+Full patch dry-run passes on the untouched base. Corrected checks use literal LF patch chunks against the index, avoiding bracket-path globs and Windows newline translation. All fourteen chunks are forward-compatible; none is wholly already applied. The earlier preflight reverse/skip finding was incorrect and is superseded by workbook-patch-compatibility.json. No patch was force-applied.
+
+Much of the proposed service/article guidance overlaps existing selection, compatibility, quotation, handover and maintenance paragraphs. Those whole extra FAQ/article sets were skipped. Historical generated reports were not imported as fresh test evidence. Regional/backlink planning was not converted into service-area claims, new offices, thin location pages, external posts or acquired links.
+
+## Implemented content and usability
+
+- Home: one concise visible service-selection answer in the existing planning section; no second planning block. Added a keyboard skip link to the focusable existing hero section.
+- Biometric: expanded the existing software/report answer with sample exports using test data and overnight-shift/missed-punch review. Preserved the three-question guide.
+- Networking: expanded an existing answer with total/per-port PoE capacity checks. No assumed product compatibility or certified testing claim.
+- AMC: expanded the existing maintenance paragraph with repair-versus-replacement quotation factors and uncertainty after inspection.
+- Contact: added outside-Lucknow availability/travel/support confirmation and advice to omit passwords/recordings/employee records in the existing intro. No area or free-visit promise was added.
+- Blogs: mapped seven existing article enquiry CTAs to real catalogue service values. Generic quote button copy replaces an unverified free-survey offer on these CTAs. Added one router-versus-switch explanation to the existing networking article. A fire-safety article enquiry resolves to the existing general Emergency Alarm System option and does not establish fire-compliance services.
+- Existing networking article: replaced unsupported 100% runtime, zero-packet-drop and Fluke certification claims with requirements/testing questions. Replaced a blanket suppression-system prescription and fixed-temperature promise with professional/equipment-specific assessment. Other historical article/project claims remain subject to the owner/editorial review noted below; no blanket fact certification is claimed.
+
+No titles, descriptions, public paths, primary H1s, canonicals, sitemap membership or schema identities changed. No keyword meta tags, hidden lists, repetitive near-me phrases, artificial location pages or new public URLs were added. Existing useful service planning content is retained.
+
+## Performance implementation
+
+Home initially renders only the critical first carousel image with high fetch priority. Invisible slides enter the request queue after the first image is loaded and the browser is idle; explicit navigation can still load a requested slide immediately. Existing carousel timing, controls and first-image dimensions remain. English is the server source, so the language helper avoids an unnecessary initial full-DOM scan/observer when no translation needs restoring. Hindi, English restoration and dynamic carousel updates are tested.
+
+The original 4-second enquiry popup and its form behavior were preserved. No analytics, consent, third-party source behavior or security setting was disabled to improve a production score. Test-only external request blocking applies equally to both isolated variants.
+
+## Complete keyword disposition
+
+workbook-keyword-disposition.csv records all 946 phrases once, original target, source row, intent, classification, action, implementation location, confirmation and validation scope. Targets on held/rejected records are source context, not approved destinations for advertising an unsupported offering. No exact phrase insertion is promised. Short synonyms, cost, near-me and Roman Hindi variants consolidate into the corresponding buyer intent rather than repeated copy.
+
+Classification counts:
+- existing page intent retained: 130
+- consolidated existing intent: 361
+- quotation intent consolidated: 66
+- owner confirmation required: 248
+- evidence confirmation required: 12
+- local intent consolidated: 46
+- question intent consolidated: 32
+- useful gap implemented: 4
+- scope confirmation required: 41
+- unsupported claim rejected: 6
+
+Four exact workbook recommendations are explicitly mapped to the newly expanded practical answers; additional Home/Contact, article handoff and claim corrections support the same existing page intents. The 130 retained core intents and other consolidated terms are not claimed as newly inserted keywords. Brand/model, repair, local-area, project and separate fire/EPABX/doorbell offerings are held or rejected where evidence is absent.
+
+## Supplied versus fresh performance evidence
+
+Provided baseline: user screenshots, production Home, 31 October 2026 around 21:13 GMT+05:30, Lighthouse 13.6.0. Mobile: score 74, FCP 1.6s, LCP 5.1s, TBT 100ms, CLS 0, Speed Index 6.4s. Desktop: score 96, FCP 0.4s, LCP 0.7s, TBT 40ms, CLS 0.021, Speed Index 2.1s. Real-user data says No data. Collapsed diagnostics give estimates, not exact resource culprits. These are provided observations, not measurements performed here.
+
+Fresh comparison: the unchanged base and proposed source were separately built with Next 16.3.5 webpack, the same reused dependency tree and synthetic loopback DB/auth configuration. Three fresh contexts per device/variant were interleaved before/after. Same installed Chrome 148 executable (provided PSI uses HeadlessChromium 153), viewport, disabled browser cache, CPU/network throttle and original popup; external traffic/non-GETs blocked on both. Local image optimisation caches and first-run variability remain in raw results. No samples were deleted.
+
+| Fresh local median | Mobile before | Mobile after | Desktop before | Desktop after |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| FCP | 1.148s | 1.216s | 0.608s | 0.552s |
+| LCP | 3.684s | 2.960s | 0.988s | 0.768s |
+| CLS | 0 | 0 | 0.00707 | 0.00707 |
+
+Mobile FCP rose by 68ms while LCP improved; samples are too few to claim statistical significance. Observed long-task blocking is recorded separately and is NOT Lighthouse TBT. No new Lighthouse score, field-data improvement, Speed Index or INP result is claimed. Local throttling (mobile 390x844, 4x CPU, 150ms/1.6Mbps; desktop 1440x900, 1x CPU, 40ms/10Mbps) differs from supplied PSI device/settings and production hosting. Re-run PageSpeed on an approved preview/release before making a production-performance claim. Four fresh screenshots and all twelve raw runs are retained.
+
+## Verification results
+
+- Baseline and proposed production webpack builds passed; 83 generated framework/static pages each, distinct from 28 canonical public pages.
+- Proposed full lint and explicit TypeScript check passed. Focused new test lint passed.
+- Five structured-data tests passed: shared business identity, actual service/provider data and safe JSON-LD.
+- Existing mocked enquiry and analytics regressions passed: address, optional email, validation, duplicate/rate limits, provider failure isolation, auth, tracking privacy/success gating and catalogue handoffs.
+- All 28 local public pages passed exact retained metadata, one expected H1, self-canonical, JSON-LD parsing/shared identity, public internal links and all thirteen service enquiry values. Local sitemap equals the rediscovered public catalogue.
+- Seven browser checks passed initially, plus the corrected Hindi restoration test. Initial test-only failure was caused by a non-ASCII selector written as question marks; a Unicode regex fixed the test and the rerun passed. Product language behavior was not weakened.
+- Two retained priority-guide/networking-article browser regressions passed; final CSV checks confirm all 946 original phrases, unique rows and validated target URLs. Ten browser checks in total passed after the test-only selector correction.
+- Fresh bounded production snapshot: six priority pages plus robots.txt and sitemap.xml returned 200; observed live sitemap count 28. Local proposed copy is not claimed deployed. No private/admin/API URL was crawled, no form submitted and no real provider triggered.
+- Mobile/desktop new content has no horizontal overflow in representative browser tests. New hero initial HTML contains one image; keyboard skip/slide navigation and Hindi-to-English restoration pass. Performance screenshots visually reviewed with the normal popup visible. This is representative coverage, not a complete device or accessibility certification.
+
+## SAGE recommendations intentionally not followed blindly
+
+No invented geo/priceRange/ratings/reviews/sameAs, fake author/date, generic FAQPage/HowTo/Speakable or WebMCP layer was added for a score. Existing openingHoursSpecification and business identity remain. Next image delivery already supports modern formats; source PNG names alone are not proof of unoptimised delivery. No blanket lazy loading of the LCP image or manual alteration of generated framework scripts. No guarantee of rich results, AI citations or rankings.
+
+## Remaining owner and account actions
+
+Resolve published PIN 227107 versus prior owner-supplied 226101 across the real office address, Maps and public records in a separate approved correction. Confirm actual travel/installation/return-visit coverage before local-area targeting; supported brands/models, repair capabilities and separate Fire Alarm/EPABX/doorbell scope; contractual AMC, spare/labour and response terms; genuine project/photo/customer permissions and historic certification/experience claims. Existing free-visit/consultation wording elsewhere needs owner substantiation; no new such offer was added here. Historical fire/safety and equipment-specific articles need qualified editorial review before reliance; this work does not certify compliance.
